--TEST--
A `spawn script` entry is a path or a static method and never an `fn` literal, `spawn worker` is not a form the parser has, and no frame keeps state that outlives it — `rule:security/isolate-values-cross-by-copy`, `rule:statements/no-function-static-and-no-global`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:concurrency/what-does-not-exist
// A literal is refused because it would carry the scope around it into a child that
// shares nothing with its parent but compiled code.
var $byLiteral = spawn script fn(): int => 1;

// `spawn worker` is not a form the parser has, so `spawn` and `worker` are read as
// two names, and neither one is declared.
var $byWorker = spawn worker "child.nvs";

// The state a fork or a thread shared has no spelling either: a frame keeps nothing
// of its own between calls, and nothing outside it is reachable.
class Counter {
    public static function next(): int {
        static $seen = 0;
        return $seen;
    }
}

global $shared;
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0802]: a `spawn script` entry is a path or a static method
%A
error: aborting due to 8 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
